{"id":"6738c8e9f2e3c32e","group":"17","path":"17/17-thm-prime-model-uniqueness.md","title":"Uniqueness of Prime Models","display":"thm-prime-model-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Prime Models","type":"theorem","metadata":{"numbering_status":"local atom identifier; not the book result number","source_section":"2.3","source_result":"Countable-language consequence of Theorems 2.3.3 and 2.3.4","source_pages_print":"98–99","source_pages_djvu":"114–115","source_verification":"OCR checked; local mathematical formulation reviewed","type":"theorem","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-thm-prime-model-uniqueness","aliases":["17-thm-prime-model-uniqueness"],"display":"thm-prime-model-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Prime Models","depends_on":["[[17-df-language-cardinality]]","[[17-df-theory-properties]]","[[17-df-prime-model]]","[[17-df-isomorphism]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-thm-7.2.1b","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"numbering_status","html":"local atom identifier; not the book result number"},{"key":"source_section","html":"2.3"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Countable-language consequence of Theorems 2.3.3 and 2.3.4"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"98–99"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"114–115"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"OCR checked; local mathematical formulation reviewed"},{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-thm-prime-model-uniqueness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-thm-prime-model-uniqueness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-prime-model-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Prime Models"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bd7acd1192e46962\" href=\"?note=bd7acd1192e46962\" title=\"17-df-theory-properties\">17-df-theory-properties</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"086b1b3d5b60a929\" href=\"?note=086b1b3d5b60a929\" title=\"17-df-prime-model\">17-df-prime-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9f3187e8ff79e64e\" href=\"?note=9f3187e8ff79e64e\" title=\"17-df-isomorphism\">17-df-isomorphism</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-thm-7.2.1b"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak Q\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\">\\(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak Q\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\)</span>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\">\\(|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\\)</span>, with language size from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"e8f9375543fc2e7d\" href=\"?note=e8f9375543fc2e7d\" title=\"17-df-language-cardinality\">17-df-language-cardinality</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Complete}\">\\(\\operatorname{Complete}\\)</span> (theory-completeness predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"bd7acd1192e46962\" href=\"?note=bd7acd1192e46962\" title=\"17-df-theory-properties\">17-df-theory-properties</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L\\)</span> (prime-model predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"086b1b3d5b60a929\" href=\"?note=086b1b3d5b60a929\" title=\"17-df-prime-model\">17-df-prime-model</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\cong\">\\(\\cong\\)</span> (structure isomorphism, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"9f3187e8ff79e64e\" href=\"?note=9f3187e8ff79e64e\" title=\"17-df-isomorphism\">17-df-isomorphism</a>)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{Complete}(T)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak P,T)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak Q,T)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\mathfrak P\\cong\\mathfrak Q.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{Complete}(T)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak P,T)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{PrimeModel}_L(\\mathfrak Q,T)\n\\Bigr)\n\\to\n\\mathfrak P\\cong\\mathfrak Q.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Whenever a complete theory in a countable language has a prime model, it is unique up to isomorphism. Mere membership of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak Q\">\\(\\mathfrak P,\\mathfrak Q\\)</span> in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> would not imply this.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-language-cardinality","status":"resolved","id":"e8f9375543fc2e7d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-